		(uuid "ff0d6f93-7ff1-59e7-b552-df7d4e94ff0e")
	)
	(text "Why: a current-source DUT cannot be held in CC (two current sources in series rail to compliance) and a firmware CV loop on the\nDAC cannot either: 1 LSB into the 2.2 uF snubber slews 11 V in one 10 ms update. Here: V_DUT below CV_SET -> U12A rises -> Q13 pulls\nV_SET down -> less current. CV_SET = 0 V: VSEN_OA (85 mV minimum) > CV_SET, U12A stays low, Q13 off, plain CC (decks 01-04).\nDeck 06: settles for 0.1 - 8 A with and without 47 uF across the DUT. Below 0.1 A it hunts: use CC or a resistor there."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18 169 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5db36de8-5ce4-5e6d-86b1-c99b446a5f79")
	)
